<title>AUSTRALIA: ANZ holds fire on A$200 mln debt issue.</title>
<headline>ANZ holds fire on A$200 mln debt issue.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd (ANZ) said on Wednesday it has delayed the pricing of its A$200 million domestic fixed rate transferable deposit issue announced on Tuesday due to market conditions.</p>
<p>An official for the bank said it was unable to achieve its benchmark target this morning as planned and was delaying the pricing until it could achieve such a target.</p>
<p>The issue was due to mature on July 15, 2000, and lead managed by ANZ Investment Bank.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
